WEBVTT

00:04.546 --> 00:06.547
THE FOLLOWING CONTENT CONTAINS DEPICTIONS
OF CHILD MALTREATMENT.

00:06.548 --> 00:07.549
VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED.

00:08.509 --> 00:10.051
-  Heeju!
-  Heeju!

00:10.052 --> 00:13.512
-  Heeju!
-  Heeju, where are you?

00:13.513 --> 00:16.266
-  Heeju!
-  Heeju! Heeju!

00:16.934 --> 00:19.352
Sunok, Sunok! Heeju!

00:24.066 --> 00:26.567
Hey, what the hell are you doing?

00:28.070 --> 00:29.946
How do we get down there?

00:31.281 --> 00:33.407
-  Heeju, it's me, Auntie Mija.
- I swear she's nothing but trouble.

00:33.408 --> 00:34.534
Right here!

00:34.535 --> 00:35.785
Are you okay?

00:35.786 --> 00:38.246
-  How can we get her out of there?
-  What do we do?

00:38.247 --> 00:40.289
You've got no idea how dangerous
this place is.

00:40.290 --> 00:42.833
Fine then, go on.
Get back in there.

00:42.834 --> 00:44.545
This woman is my mother.

00:45.629 --> 00:47.756
"Nothing but bad luck."

00:48.799 --> 00:51.134
That's what my mom always called me.

00:52.386 --> 00:55.222
I thought my mom's misfortune
was because of me.

00:56.306 --> 00:58.267
And so I always felt guilty.

00:59.351 --> 01:02.144
At the time,
I didn't understand what that meant.

01:23.333 --> 01:25.669
Spellbound by
the dazzling lights...

01:26.503 --> 01:29.297
...people streamed endlessly
toward Gold Land.

01:32.634 --> 01:35.678
They say not everything that glitters
is gold.

01:35.679 --> 01:39.474
In the end,
it was nothing more than a gilded grave.

01:49.109 --> 01:52.778
Maybe my mother was dazzled
by those lights, too,

01:52.779 --> 01:55.489
wagering everything she had.

01:55.490 --> 01:57.199
Player, banker.

01:57.200 --> 01:58.869
Hoping for
a single stroke of luck.

02:01.163 --> 02:05.459
Unfortunately, luck is never fair, is it?

02:06.543 --> 02:08.003
Final bets.

02:11.340 --> 02:12.923
- Ah.
-  Out.

02:12.924 --> 02:14.383
You fold?

02:14.384 --> 02:16.677
- House wins.
-  I can't believe this.

02:23.185 --> 02:28.357
13, JEONGSAN BUS TERMINAL
SEOKWOL-DONG

02:40.285 --> 02:41.994
Did you eat yet?

02:41.995 --> 02:42.996
Ramyeon.

02:57.969 --> 02:59.513
I wanna go to school, Mom.

03:00.514 --> 03:04.518
Da In gets to go to school
and she's a year younger than me.

03:07.104 --> 03:08.355
You can go next year.

03:10.565 --> 03:11.608
Not here, though.

03:12.901 --> 03:14.902
You can go in Seoul.

03:14.903 --> 03:16.363
Really?

03:17.864 --> 03:20.283
Yes. Really.

03:22.994 --> 03:25.163
I just can't live in
this place any longer.
:cue

03:27.249 --> 03:28.458
We'll go to Seoul.

03:33.922 --> 03:36.675
As always, it was just a lie.

03:38.385 --> 03:42.138
But even if it was a lie,
I wanted to believe it.

03:42.139 --> 03:45.015
THE CITY OF DREAMS AND HOPE
WELCOME TO GOLD LAND

03:45.016 --> 03:48.644
HIGH-VALUE LOANS, HAENGBOK PAWNSHOP
LENDING, PURCHASING

03:48.645 --> 03:54.942
GOLD, SILVER, JEWELRY, WATCHES
TOP PRICES PAID FOR GOLD

03:54.943 --> 03:58.112
-  Come here.
-  Instead of leaving like she said,

03:58.113 --> 04:00.656
my mother got married
to the pawnshop owner.

04:00.657 --> 04:04.702
On the condition
that he paid off her debt.

04:04.703 --> 04:09.666
Both me and my mother
were like collateral at his shop.

04:10.584 --> 04:14.336
I said cut it out.

04:14.337 --> 04:16.881
Slow down.
Be careful, kids.

04:24.681 --> 04:29.686
A heart with no destination
to go always lets the feet know first.

04:31.730 --> 04:33.731
For many years I was stuck,

04:33.732 --> 04:36.735
walking down a road I never wanted
to return to.

04:37.861 --> 04:42.199
I prayed every day that my destination
would be somewhere else.

04:43.784 --> 04:48.037
In reality, the dream
that felt so far away

04:48.038 --> 04:51.082
only grew closer and more familiar.

04:51.917 --> 04:56.213
♪ All the things
I thought I could be ♪

04:57.422 --> 04:59.674
♪ Wild and free ♪

05:01.885 --> 05:06.430
♪ Leave it all behind ♪

05:06.431 --> 05:10.726
♪ As you fall in line ♪

05:10.727 --> 05:14.980
♪ I'm not expecting any laughter ♪

05:14.981 --> 05:16.857
♪ There's nothing left ♪

05:16.858 --> 05:22.947
♪ Just the pieces of everything
we could have been before ♪

05:22.948 --> 05:26.660
♪ Evermore ♪

05:27.494 --> 05:33.082
♪ I don't feel it like I used to ♪

05:33.083 --> 05:35.627
♪ Anymore ♪

05:39.005 --> 05:43.425
My mother was like a plant
that could no longer bloom,

05:43.426 --> 05:44.761
slowly withering away.

05:46.513 --> 05:48.557
The thought that I could end up
like her...

05:50.267 --> 05:51.434
...It terrified me.

05:52.811 --> 05:55.981
♪ Still calling through
the night ♪

05:57.399 --> 06:01.193
♪ I leave behind all of the seasons... ♪

06:01.194 --> 06:04.781
At Haengbok Pawnshop,
there is no happiness.

06:06.449 --> 06:10.077
Only someone's collateral,
held like hostages.

06:11.955 --> 06:14.249
If only I could
fly somewhere else.

06:15.166 --> 06:16.418
How nice would it be?

06:17.127 --> 06:18.419
Anywhere.

06:18.420 --> 06:20.130
Anywhere but here.

06:21.923 --> 06:24.217
♪ On your own ♪

06:25.719 --> 06:27.094
Sometimes in the evenings,

06:27.095 --> 06:29.722
the pawnshop became
a gambling den.

06:38.523 --> 06:41.400
Soju there, cigarettes here.
We have to sell it all.

06:41.401 --> 06:43.069
Bring it here!

06:49.534 --> 06:50.535
:cue

08:17.706 --> 08:18.956
Mr. Han.

08:18.957 --> 08:20.874
I said I'd give it to you by next week!

08:20.875 --> 08:22.085
So you keep saying.

08:23.086 --> 08:25.588
I trust money, not words.

08:26.339 --> 08:29.675
People say they'll
pay back billions, even trillions.

08:35.849 --> 08:37.600
What's wrong?

08:38.268 --> 08:40.352
Is your little heart pounding?

08:40.353 --> 08:43.564
I could cut you open
for screwing me out of my money.

08:43.565 --> 08:45.233
Is that what
you're worried about?

08:57.704 --> 09:00.664
Look here.
You see that?

09:00.665 --> 09:03.792
It's easy to control
it when it's my own flesh.

09:03.793 --> 09:07.337
But on someone else's,
not so much.

09:07.338 --> 09:12.009
That's why I always cut myself first
to show you.

10:01.810 --> 10:03.186
What are you doing here?

10:06.147 --> 10:08.023
Just my homework.

10:08.024 --> 10:09.109
I guess I fell asleep.

10:10.026 --> 10:12.070
Oh, really?

10:19.702 --> 10:22.329
:cue

10:35.844 --> 10:37.970
Heeju!

11:02.245 --> 11:04.621
-  Where are you?
-  I'm leaving this place.

11:04.622 --> 11:08.375
I won't go back. That man is crazy.
He's not even human. I'm too scared to.

11:08.376 --> 11:09.627
Where else would you go?

11:10.295 --> 11:12.505
Anywhere. I don't know.

11:13.381 --> 11:15.299
You got any money?

11:15.300 --> 11:16.926
How are you gonna survive on your own?

11:17.802 --> 11:20.554
I don't know.
I'll figure it out.

11:20.555 --> 11:23.056
And you?
You're okay living like this?

11:23.057 --> 11:25.268
You actually think he sees me
as his niece?

11:26.936 --> 11:28.897
Go and stay with Mija for a while.

11:29.689 --> 11:32.107
When your uncle cools off,
you can come back.

11:34.235 --> 11:37.780
No, Mom, why can't we
just leave this place?

11:39.782 --> 11:40.783
Don't call me Mom.

11:44.829 --> 11:46.331
Oh, that's right.

11:47.582 --> 11:48.875
I don't have a mother.

11:50.335 --> 11:52.085
I almost forgot.

11:52.086 --> 11:57.133
I'm nothing but an utterly luckless brat.

13:03.825 --> 13:11.165
EPISODE 2
HOMECOMING

13:44.282 --> 13:46.116
Uh, hi there.

13:46.117 --> 13:51.122
Last night there was a car accident on
National Route 6 around midnight, I think.

13:52.040 --> 13:54.709
Have there been any reports
of the accident yet?
:cue

14:00.757 --> 14:02.841
Could you tell me what hospital he's in?

14:02.842 --> 14:05.511
May I have
the name of the person calling?

14:06.429 --> 14:07.430
I...

14:24.155 --> 14:25.406
There isn't?

14:25.907 --> 14:27.324
Okay, thank you.

14:33.664 --> 14:35.582
Hello.

14:35.583 --> 14:38.502
I'm calling to check on a patient who
was brought to the ER after

14:38.503 --> 14:41.088
a car accident around midnight last night.
It's a man...

14:41.089 --> 14:43.673
Hey, Heeju!
Heeju!

14:43.674 --> 14:45.051
They want all of us in the office.

14:45.551 --> 14:46.635
Why?

14:46.636 --> 14:48.178
The police
are here now.

14:48.179 --> 14:50.097
They have some questions for all of us.

14:50.098 --> 14:52.307
Ms. Cha, too.
We gotta go.

14:52.308 --> 14:53.309
Sure.

15:00.942 --> 15:02.276
What is that?

15:03.277 --> 15:05.238
That can't be normal, can it?

15:06.656 --> 15:10.117
Yesterday, who was-who was in charge
of the scanner?

15:10.118 --> 15:12.160
Uh, I was.

15:12.161 --> 15:14.329
The warning alarm went off, right?

15:14.330 --> 15:16.665
Aren't you supposed to request
a physical inspection from customs?

15:16.666 --> 15:20.043
Uh, sir, well...

15:20.044 --> 15:21.586
She reported it to me.

15:21.587 --> 15:24.005
As the one in charge, I review
all anomalies and make the final call.

15:24.006 --> 15:27.384
A visual inspection by an expert
is considered the most accurate method.

15:27.385 --> 15:29.344
The alarms are always going off.

15:29.345 --> 15:30.971
And for inbound cargo,

15:30.972 --> 15:33.181
physical inspections
are deemed unnecessary unless

15:33.182 --> 15:34.266
it's an emergency.

15:34.267 --> 15:36.184
This is because it's already been through

15:36.185 --> 15:38.603
a thorough screening
at the outbound checkpoint,

15:38.604 --> 15:40.897
especially when transporting a casket
with a dead body.

15:42.150 --> 15:44.317
So what kind of goods

15:44.318 --> 15:46.319
were they supposedly smuggling?

15:46.320 --> 15:48.613
Ma'am, we never said anything
about smuggling.

15:48.614 --> 15:51.909
The police wouldn't be making such
a fuss if it was for anything else.

15:53.161 --> 15:55.370
Look, you all know this man, right?

15:55.371 --> 15:57.164
San Air first officer Lee Dokyung.

15:57.165 --> 15:59.624
Yeah, I've seen him around a few times.

15:59.625 --> 16:01.126
Have you been
in touch recently?

16:01.127 --> 16:02.502
Maybe the last few days?

16:02.503 --> 16:03.753
No.

16:03.754 --> 16:05.006
What about everyone else?

16:07.800 --> 16:11.261
This airport's tiny, so,
weird no one knows him.

16:11.262 --> 16:15.932
Are you asking about the captain because
he's somehow connected to all this?

16:15.933 --> 16:18.268
No, not quite.
It's not like that.

16:18.269 --> 16:19.478
Oh.

16:20.938 --> 16:23.940
Heeju, you were working
at the arrivals terminal.

16:23.941 --> 16:25.317
You must know him.

16:25.318 --> 16:27.195
You would have handled security
for inbound crew.

16:28.946 --> 16:30.030
Yeah.

16:30.031 --> 16:31.448
I see.

16:31.449 --> 16:32.867
Have you been in contact recently?

16:33.701 --> 16:37.746
Well, it's not like we keep in touch
or anything like that.

16:37.747 --> 16:40.498
We just say hello when
he went through security.

16:40.499 --> 16:41.750
Understood.

16:41.751 --> 16:43.335
- It's Dokyung. They found him.
- Well, where is he?

16:43.336 --> 16:44.961
He's at Yangpo Jeil Hospital.

16:44.962 --> 16:47.130
All right,
thanks everyone.

16:47.131 --> 16:48.507
We'll be in touch.

16:57.475 --> 16:58.476
Heeju, wait a minute.

17:00.478 --> 17:02.562
Can I speak with you?

17:13.449 --> 17:14.783
Prep the patient
for surgery.

17:14.784 --> 17:15.785
Yes, Doctor.
:cue

17:20.790 --> 17:23.459
So how long have you been close
with Lee Dokyung?

17:24.627 --> 17:25.835
What?

17:25.836 --> 17:27.296
This isn't your first time, is it?

17:28.422 --> 17:30.091
Smuggling goods.

17:31.008 --> 17:33.843
Uh, Ms. Cha, I'm not sure exactly
what you're trying to say.

17:33.844 --> 17:34.970
Fine.

17:34.971 --> 17:36.638
First time or not,

17:36.639 --> 17:38.890
keep your mouth shut
and pretend you don't know anything.

17:38.891 --> 17:42.686
If you're caught by the police,
you understand you and I are both done?

17:48.526 --> 17:50.860
Send me your resignation letter tonight.

17:50.861 --> 17:52.821
And don't come into work tomorrow.

17:52.822 --> 17:55.616
I'll talk to the company
and sort things out.

17:56.826 --> 17:59.828
Once the police wrap up
their investigation,

17:59.829 --> 18:01.080
someone will have to take the fall.

18:01.914 --> 18:04.207
I don't know what's going on
between you two,

18:04.208 --> 18:05.418
but our best hope...

18:07.503 --> 18:10.339
...Is that Lee Dokyung goes and dies.

18:38.576 --> 18:40.786
Is Mr. Lee Dokyung's
guardian here?

18:41.537 --> 18:42.580
Here.

18:43.080 --> 18:44.498
Looks like
the surgery went well.

18:45.416 --> 18:47.500
Mr. Lee is now in recovery.

18:47.501 --> 18:49.587
He's in room 3103.

18:50.880 --> 18:52.589
Is he awake yet?

18:52.590 --> 18:53.966
Uh...

19:00.181 --> 19:01.973
It usually takes about an hour

19:01.974 --> 19:05.769
or two for the anesthesia to wear off,
so he's still asleep.

19:05.770 --> 19:07.687
You can't see him yet.

19:07.688 --> 19:09.565
Sir, he still needs to rest!

19:51.732 --> 19:52.941
Yeah.

19:52.942 --> 19:54.984
Yeah, I'll head down
to the first floor.

19:54.985 --> 19:56.028
Okay.

20:13.129 --> 20:14.380
Dokyung.

20:16.590 --> 20:18.342
Wake up.
It's me, Heeju.

20:19.009 --> 20:20.261
Dokyung, can you hear me?

20:23.514 --> 20:24.557
Dokyung.

20:29.520 --> 20:31.230
Dokyung, can you hear me?

20:38.237 --> 20:40.238
Heeju.

20:40.239 --> 20:42.700
I told you not to come here,
didn't I?

20:43.242 --> 20:45.285
I said I'd contact you.

20:45.286 --> 20:47.204
It's okay.
I managed to sneak in.

20:50.666 --> 20:51.917
And the van?

20:53.252 --> 20:54.961
Don't worry. I hid it.

20:54.962 --> 20:56.881
Somewhere no one will know.

20:57.506 --> 20:59.048
- Where's that?
-  In Jeongsan,

20:59.049 --> 21:00.842
in the abandoned mines.
:cue

21:00.843 --> 21:03.846
I left it deep in the tunnels
where no one goes anymore.

21:10.686 --> 21:11.687
You did it.

21:12.772 --> 21:13.981
You did it, Heeju.

21:16.358 --> 21:18.360
I'll take care of everything from here.

21:19.111 --> 21:20.279
You should go now.

21:21.155 --> 21:22.615
I'm okay. You can go.

21:25.242 --> 21:27.703
The police came to the airport today.

21:28.829 --> 21:30.080
The police? Why?

21:31.832 --> 21:36.044
Well, it looks like they think you were
involved in smuggling in that casket,

21:36.045 --> 21:39.089
and they also know you're in the hospital
because of a car accident. Also...

21:40.633 --> 21:43.718
...those men who hit you with the car,

21:43.719 --> 21:44.845
they're here waiting for you.
I saw them.

21:47.848 --> 21:48.932
Let's turn ourselves in.

21:48.933 --> 21:51.226
If we confess to the police now,

21:51.227 --> 21:52.811
the charges might not be that bad.

21:52.812 --> 21:54.355
The police aren't the problem, Heeju.

21:56.732 --> 21:58.734
It's the men you saw outside.

22:00.027 --> 22:02.279
If I were to tell the police
where their drugs are located...

22:03.197 --> 22:05.490
- ...Those guys would...
- But it's not drugs.

22:05.491 --> 22:07.158
What?

22:07.159 --> 22:09.285
That's not what's in the casket.

22:09.286 --> 22:11.162
It's not drugs at all.

22:11.163 --> 22:13.833
Then what is it?

22:15.251 --> 22:16.502
Gold bars.

22:18.671 --> 22:22.298
There are a whole bunch of gold bars
that say 10 kilograms on them.

22:22.299 --> 22:24.468
I didn't count,
but there has to be 100.

22:26.929 --> 22:30.683
100 ten-kilogram gold bars?

22:31.559 --> 22:32.726
You're positive?

22:33.978 --> 22:36.771
-  Did you see them yourself?
- Yeah.

22:36.772 --> 22:38.148
Wait a minute.

22:41.193 --> 22:44.947
You mean-you mean there's a ton of gold?

22:47.157 --> 22:49.742
But we should just return it.

22:49.743 --> 22:51.286
If they'll go this far to get it,

22:51.287 --> 22:53.330
then you should just give
it back to them, right?

22:54.874 --> 22:58.334
We can tell the police that you didn't
know what was in the casket because

22:58.335 --> 22:59.419
you really didn't know, right?

22:59.420 --> 23:01.754
No, Heeju.
Wait, wait, wait, Heeju.

23:01.755 --> 23:03.966
Wait a minute.
Wait a minute.

23:05.384 --> 23:10.806
So you're completely sure no one
knows that you hid the van in the mines?

23:20.941 --> 23:23.818
JEONGSAN BUS TERMINAL

23:31.535 --> 23:32.536
Heeju.

23:34.288 --> 23:36.165
Don't tell anyone where the casket is.

23:37.374 --> 23:38.918
No one but the two of us can know.

23:40.002 --> 23:41.754
I won't tell anyone, either.

23:43.339 --> 23:45.132
I swear I'll keep it a secret.

23:46.050 --> 23:47.092
No matter what.

23:48.469 --> 23:50.387
Even with a knife to my throat.

24:11.825 --> 24:15.204
From now on,
this is our whole lives.

24:19.375 --> 24:21.043
I'm gonna turn myself in.

24:22.294 --> 24:24.213
If the police can't find the gold bars...

24:25.506 --> 24:26.507
...I could get out in a year.

24:27.675 --> 24:30.636
With a good lawyer I could
even get a suspended sentence.

24:31.679 --> 24:34.139
You're gonna have to keep
the gold safe for us, Heeju.

24:34.932 --> 24:36.266
Until I can get out.
:cue

25:13.303 --> 25:18.182
DAD! BE SAFE AGAIN TODAY

25:29.278 --> 25:31.655
First, bury the gold bars
in the mine...

25:32.489 --> 25:34.616
...so that if anyone goes in,
they won't see them.

25:45.252 --> 25:46.627
Move them one at a time.

25:46.628 --> 25:48.047
I know you can do it.

25:49.048 --> 25:50.298
It will take a while.

25:52.051 --> 25:53.469
But please bury them.

27:06.834 --> 27:09.293
Take the van back
to the abandoned warehouse.

27:09.294 --> 27:10.587
The one from that night.

27:19.263 --> 27:21.640
Make sure you don't
leave fingerprints or anything.

27:22.933 --> 27:26.895
That way even if the police find the van,
it won't matter.

27:27.855 --> 27:29.106
They can't trace it to you.

27:38.490 --> 27:40.367
Find a place
to lay low for a while.

27:41.577 --> 27:42.703
Don't try to contact me.

27:43.453 --> 27:44.705
Don't even look for me.

27:46.665 --> 27:50.961
I will find a way
to contact you if it's necessary.

28:16.111 --> 28:17.988
Hey, Captain.
:cue

28:19.114 --> 28:21.074
It's me, Park.

28:29.291 --> 28:31.460
Ah, open your eyes.

28:32.210 --> 28:33.503
I know you're awake.

28:40.302 --> 28:42.220
You look like you're gonna piss yourself.

28:46.934 --> 28:49.352
How did a little bitch
like you pull this off?

28:49.353 --> 28:50.562
Why'd you do it?

28:51.730 --> 28:55.274
You upset?
Did I somehow upset you?

28:55.275 --> 28:58.736
Up until now,
we always got along.

28:58.737 --> 29:00.781
You that desperate for cash?

29:02.240 --> 29:04.116
Money always screws things up.

29:04.117 --> 29:05.410
I understand.

29:07.454 --> 29:10.081
Well, I guess I'm
the one who put you here,

29:10.082 --> 29:11.833
so I'm partly to blame.

29:13.293 --> 29:16.045
Let's go back
to the original deal.

29:16.046 --> 29:18.882
The casket for 200 million.

29:19.591 --> 29:22.593
Ah, it's fine.
You don't need to say anything.

29:25.305 --> 29:26.556
This is your phone, right?

29:29.893 --> 29:31.478
Your partner,
the one who took off with the van?

29:32.270 --> 29:33.313
Call him.

29:34.356 --> 29:36.733
Found his burner phone.
The real one.

29:38.026 --> 29:39.027
Now, which is it?

29:41.071 --> 29:42.072
Huh?

29:43.073 --> 29:45.574
All you need is a finger.
Just press it, you little...

29:45.575 --> 29:47.035
You really expect me to trust you?

29:48.620 --> 29:50.872
You might kill me after I return
the casket.

29:52.624 --> 29:53.875
You already tried to
kill me once.

29:56.503 --> 29:57.963
Yeah, I know.

29:59.131 --> 30:01.173
Why did I do that?

30:01.174 --> 30:02.634
Deposit one billion won into my account.

30:03.802 --> 30:04.970
Get all these cops off my tail.

30:05.971 --> 30:07.431
And get me out of the country.

30:09.808 --> 30:11.600
Then I'll tell you where the casket is.

30:11.601 --> 30:13.728
Like I can trust you.

30:15.981 --> 30:18.108
I've got nothin' to tell you, then.

30:19.067 --> 30:20.360
Okay.

30:22.571 --> 30:24.239
Heard you got 22 stitches.

30:25.157 --> 30:26.240
Let's open 'em up!

30:28.076 --> 30:31.287
Just one fucking phone call
and this'd be over.

30:31.288 --> 30:34.749
You should have called when I
was being nice, you stupid fuck!

30:36.126 --> 30:37.794
Sir!

30:45.135 --> 30:46.762
Better take care of yourself.

30:48.263 --> 30:50.306
I'll be back soon, Captain.

31:16.041 --> 31:22.047
HAENGBOK PAWNSHOP

31:35.143 --> 31:36.603
We're closed.

31:41.191 --> 31:42.733
What's going on?

31:42.734 --> 31:44.528
What are you doing here?

31:48.115 --> 31:50.449
I'm just gonna stay here for a little.

31:50.450 --> 31:51.951
A few days.

31:51.952 --> 31:54.912
Well, maybe a month.

31:54.913 --> 31:56.456
What about work?

31:57.374 --> 32:01.502
I quit, so it'll only be until
I find something else.
:cue

32:01.503 --> 32:03.045
Don't worry. It won't be long.

32:03.046 --> 32:05.090
You said you'd never come back.

32:06.758 --> 32:09.427
Guess you found out the real world
isn't so easy, huh?

32:11.972 --> 32:15.391
That's what life is like for women
with nothing to offer but their body.

32:15.392 --> 32:18.435
I didn't live like you did, Auntie.

32:18.436 --> 32:19.437
Then why'd you crawl back here?

32:20.522 --> 32:22.940
You say it's temporary but you can't
even afford a hotel?

32:22.941 --> 32:24.191
And what about you?

32:24.192 --> 32:25.819
Are you still living with
a man who beats you?

32:29.906 --> 32:32.117
Forget it.
I'll get a hotel.

32:32.617 --> 32:34.535
If it's really only
for a little while,

32:34.536 --> 32:36.580
you can stay here.

32:40.709 --> 32:41.960
I said you can stay.

32:46.339 --> 32:47.591
Have you eaten?

32:48.550 --> 32:50.802
It's fine.
I'll take care of myself.

32:51.636 --> 32:53.305
I'll just come back here to sleep.

32:55.015 --> 32:58.185
Is that, uh, gambling den still here?

33:00.145 --> 33:02.105
Nope. We had to stop.

33:03.231 --> 33:05.065
We got raided, so...

33:05.066 --> 33:08.612
- Then what is he up to now?
- I don't know.

33:09.613 --> 33:10.697
He barely comes home these days.

33:11.907 --> 33:13.200
That's a good thing.

33:14.201 --> 33:15.659
I don't want him to know I'm here.

33:15.660 --> 33:17.161
Don't tell anyone else, either.

33:17.162 --> 33:19.623
No one around here
is asking about you.

33:20.582 --> 33:21.583
Where are you going?

33:22.334 --> 33:24.084
I'm getting sheets for you.

33:24.085 --> 33:25.753
You're gonna have to sleep in the vault.

33:25.754 --> 33:29.382
The latch is broken,
so make sure you lock the front door.

33:30.467 --> 33:32.344
Oh, look at you.

33:34.012 --> 33:35.763
The bags under your eyes
look awful.

33:35.764 --> 33:37.015
And what's on your hands?

33:39.601 --> 33:40.560
What the hell have you been doing?

33:43.021 --> 33:45.232
Oh, forget it.

34:12.092 --> 34:14.594
When this goes to court,
I'll need an expensive lawyer.

34:15.136 --> 34:16.470
And money for bail.

34:16.471 --> 34:18.222
GOLD BAR

34:18.223 --> 34:21.351
We can sell one gold bar
and use that to cover expenses.

34:22.644 --> 34:24.271
Okay, how?

34:25.730 --> 34:28.274
There must be a way to do it.

34:28.275 --> 34:30.150
See what you can find out.
I'll look into it, too.

34:30.151 --> 34:31.110
HOW TO BUY AND SELL
A 75-GRAM GOLD BAR?

34:31.111 --> 34:32.028
WHAT IS A 75-GRAM GOLD BAR?

34:41.705 --> 34:42.747
Heeju.

34:43.790 --> 34:45.708
When I get out of prison,

34:45.709 --> 34:49.296
the first thing we'll do is sell all
the gold bars and get outta here.

34:50.630 --> 34:52.465
Maybe France or wherever.

34:53.508 --> 34:54.759
Somewhere no one
will ever find us.

34:56.428 --> 34:59.139
This is a once in a lifetime opportunity
for us, Heeju.

35:00.181 --> 35:02.683
It could completely change our lives.

35:02.684 --> 35:03.935
You can do this.

35:19.284 --> 35:22.287
:cue

35:40.930 --> 35:42.807
Have you ever seen this van before, sir?

35:44.267 --> 35:45.684
No, I've never seen it before.

35:45.685 --> 35:47.269
There's no van like that
in the neighborhood,

35:47.270 --> 35:48.520
so I have no idea how it got there.

35:48.521 --> 35:50.439
Do you have any injuries?

35:50.440 --> 35:51.815
I mean, I'm not hurt anywhere.

35:51.816 --> 35:53.150
But look at this.

35:53.151 --> 35:55.694
When I got here,
everything was a mess.

35:55.695 --> 35:58.072
It looks like someone crashed
and left the van here.

35:58.073 --> 36:01.868
We found the van, sir,
with the 9900 plate.

36:02.535 --> 36:04.746
Casket?
There's no casket here.

36:05.705 --> 36:08.415
- What do you wanna eat?
- I dunno.

36:08.416 --> 36:09.792
Ah, shit.

36:09.793 --> 36:11.835
I'm starving.

36:11.836 --> 36:14.963
They found the van,
but the casket's not in there.

36:14.964 --> 36:17.591
Lee Dokyung keeps denying
that he knows anything about it.

36:17.592 --> 36:19.636
- For now, at least.
-  Good work.

36:20.845 --> 36:22.764
Come to the hotel soon.
We'll grab food.

36:31.439 --> 36:35.359
All the men we sent to the airport,
you picked them out yourself, right?

36:35.360 --> 36:36.902
Yeah.

36:36.903 --> 36:39.406
You specifically told me to pick out
the smartest and strongest.

36:40.407 --> 36:42.241
Lee Dokyung didn't act on his own.

36:42.242 --> 36:44.493
There's someone else.

36:44.494 --> 36:46.370
Ah!

36:46.371 --> 36:49.289
I already told you,
it's not one of my boys!

36:49.290 --> 36:51.251
I think...

36:53.378 --> 36:54.421
You wanted to see me?

37:00.593 --> 37:03.012
Hand over your phone.
You gotta unlock it.

37:13.314 --> 37:14.774
Where'd you hide the casket?

37:15.859 --> 37:16.984
What?

37:16.985 --> 37:19.653
You were the one who drove the van
from Yangpo Airport.

37:19.654 --> 37:22.741
Uh, I already told my boss all about it.

37:24.200 --> 37:25.869
That shit head pilot.

37:26.786 --> 37:28.788
Uh, Lee Dokyung, he...

37:29.414 --> 37:31.750
...he pulled out a gun
and held it to my head.

37:32.459 --> 37:34.168
He took off with the van.

37:34.169 --> 37:38.715
But that night, the first person
to find our missing van was you.

37:39.466 --> 37:40.549
You.

37:40.550 --> 37:43.844
And you were the only one
who saw the driver's face.

37:43.845 --> 37:46.306
Aren't you gonna tell me who it was?

37:47.265 --> 37:50.143
Uh, yeah, I mean...

37:51.519 --> 37:53.896
I did my best to try and get
a good look.

37:53.897 --> 37:55.439
It-it was just so dark, though.

37:55.440 --> 37:56.566
Yeah, and the casket?

37:57.233 --> 37:58.317
Sir.

37:58.318 --> 38:00.903
I don't know.
I-I swear it wasn't me.

38:00.904 --> 38:04.282
I-I passed out yesterday 'cause I
was all beat up.

38:13.333 --> 38:15.751
Hey, boss. This isn't right.

38:15.752 --> 38:17.545
Get your fucking hands off.

38:23.468 --> 38:26.887
I already know everything
so either confess or lose an ear.

38:26.888 --> 38:29.389
Sir, I dunno. I promise.

38:29.390 --> 38:31.308
I'm telling the truth.
I swear I'm telling you...

38:31.309 --> 38:32.810
Lee Dokyung already told the police
you helped him,

38:32.811 --> 38:33.852
so just tell me where it is!

38:35.313 --> 38:37.981
This is your last chance
to confess, you asshole!

38:37.982 --> 38:39.650
You serious?

38:39.651 --> 38:41.568
Woogy, you shit.
You tell him where it is now!

38:41.569 --> 38:43.570
No, I don't know anything! Ah!

38:44.989 --> 38:48.242
Please don't kill me! Please!

38:53.957 --> 38:55.582
Get the fuck out of my sight.

38:55.583 --> 38:58.086
Fuck!

39:06.010 --> 39:07.095
I'll get going, sir.
:cue

39:16.938 --> 39:18.814
It's not him?

39:18.815 --> 39:21.733
Well, what the hell was that all about, then?

39:21.734 --> 39:25.613
Lee Dokyung did have an accomplice,
and that person hid the casket.

39:26.656 --> 39:29.283
I had to make sure that
it wasn't one of our guys.

39:29.284 --> 39:31.243
What are you gonna do?

39:32.537 --> 39:34.956
Seems like finding the casket
isn't even our biggest problem.

39:38.376 --> 39:39.794
Does the chairman know?

39:45.216 --> 39:47.759
I'm sorry.

39:47.760 --> 39:49.344
Must be really tough on you.

39:49.345 --> 39:53.599
Didn't he say once he wraps up
in Cambodia and returns to Gold Land,

39:53.600 --> 39:55.309
he'd hand over the hotel
and everything else to you?

39:55.310 --> 39:58.353
You really should do your best not
to upset him right now.

39:58.354 --> 39:59.813
Fucker!

39:59.814 --> 40:01.733
You need to shut it.

40:08.948 --> 40:10.700
You can murder just about anyone.

40:12.035 --> 40:14.537
The chairman will forgive you for that,
but if you lose his money...

40:15.330 --> 40:16.539
That's a different story.

40:17.916 --> 40:19.083
What are you gonna do?

40:19.918 --> 40:21.336
He'll be coming back soon.

41:36.828 --> 41:38.413
Come on in.

41:41.874 --> 41:43.292
Hmm.

41:45.545 --> 41:46.838
Are you here to sell?

41:48.673 --> 41:51.717
Oh. I'm guessing you don't recognize me.

41:51.718 --> 41:55.179
I used to live in Bukju, too.
The old mining town there.

41:57.473 --> 41:58.474
No?

41:59.434 --> 42:00.809
Really?

42:00.810 --> 42:03.354
Everyone tells me I look
just like when I was a kid.

42:04.313 --> 42:06.315
I guess you don't remember.

42:07.483 --> 42:08.776
So, tell me.

42:09.736 --> 42:11.069
Is Heeju with you?

42:11.070 --> 42:14.364
I heard she went to Seoul
a while ago, but is she back now?

42:14.365 --> 42:15.991
She's not.

42:15.992 --> 42:19.244
Oh, she's not? Hmm.
Thought I saw her.

42:20.830 --> 42:22.247
Heeju's not here.

42:22.248 --> 42:23.666
I doubt she's ever coming back.

42:24.834 --> 42:25.918
So pawn something or get out.

42:28.337 --> 42:31.256
Yeah, sure. Got a business to run.

42:33.259 --> 42:34.342
See ya!

42:34.343 --> 42:36.386
:cue

42:47.774 --> 42:49.983
DONGHWA JEWELRY

42:49.984 --> 42:52.736
Did you say a 10-kilogram gold bar?

42:52.737 --> 42:54.738
Uh, I don't really have anything that big.

42:54.739 --> 42:56.323
There's not really a market for that.

42:56.324 --> 42:57.949
I mean, I guess if someone

42:57.950 --> 43:01.328
really wanted one,
it could be made to order, but...

43:01.329 --> 43:03.371
- How much would it cost?
-  Right now?

43:03.372 --> 43:06.166
With our economy the way it is,
the current price of gold is pretty high.

43:06.167 --> 43:08.752
A kilo could go up to 150 million,

43:08.753 --> 43:12.422
so ten kilos is 1.5 billion.

43:13.424 --> 43:14.466
Mm.

43:14.467 --> 43:16.969
So, how much...

43:18.137 --> 43:20.890
...do you think someone would be able
to sell it for?

43:22.517 --> 43:25.602
Well, first I gotta make sure
it's pure gold.

43:25.603 --> 43:27.145
So I'd need to get a look at it.

43:27.146 --> 43:31.942
If it is pure, then I'd consider
offering 1.3 or 4 billion.

43:31.943 --> 43:34.945
I know, market price is higher than that.

43:34.946 --> 43:37.656
Are you saying you have a 10-kilogram bar

43:37.657 --> 43:39.407
of pure gold you're looking to sell?

43:39.408 --> 43:41.744
Uh, no, I don't.

43:43.454 --> 43:44.913
Just curious.

43:44.914 --> 43:46.374
Just go.

43:47.750 --> 43:48.960
You're wasting my time, young lady.

44:24.328 --> 44:28.748
BEER, LIQUOR, MIJA

44:29.917 --> 44:30.918
Who is it?

44:32.920 --> 44:34.921
Hold on.
I haven't even opened yet.

44:37.508 --> 44:39.009
Heeju?

44:39.010 --> 44:41.136
Wh-what are you doing here?

44:42.513 --> 44:43.847
Auntie, how are you?

44:43.848 --> 44:46.641
Oh, same old, same old!

44:46.642 --> 44:48.852
This way. Oh!

44:48.853 --> 44:50.854
Look at you. Sit down!

44:53.316 --> 44:55.358
Excuse the mess.
I was just eating.

44:55.359 --> 44:56.693
Have you eaten yet?

44:56.694 --> 44:57.695
Yeah.

44:59.155 --> 45:00.573
Oh, it's been so long.

45:01.532 --> 45:03.241
When'd you come back?
You here to stay?

45:03.242 --> 45:05.452
No, just here a little while.

45:05.453 --> 45:06.745
You brat.

45:06.746 --> 45:08.830
You never even called me once.

45:08.831 --> 45:10.415
I'm sorry, Auntie.

45:10.416 --> 45:12.792
I was busy trying to make a living.

45:12.793 --> 45:13.794
Yeah, of course you were.

45:16.380 --> 45:17.632
So how are you really doing?

45:19.217 --> 45:20.384
Well...

45:22.303 --> 45:23.304
...would you...

45:24.263 --> 45:28.059
...could you maybe lend me some money?

45:29.060 --> 45:30.102
How much you need?

45:32.355 --> 45:35.566
It's kind of a lot.
50 million won or so.

45:37.068 --> 45:39.277
I could pay it back really quickly, though.

45:39.278 --> 45:40.487
I'll have it in a month or so.

45:40.488 --> 45:42.864
Things haven't been easy for you,
either, have they?

45:46.494 --> 45:48.537
Of course you need money.

45:49.914 --> 45:51.749
Sunok's cancer,
I know all about it.

45:53.709 --> 45:57.128
I mean, I tried to get her
to go to the hospital, but she won't go.

45:57.129 --> 45:59.590
She said she can barely afford food
for herself.

46:00.633 --> 46:02.133
I don't even think
your uncle knows.

46:02.134 --> 46:04.053
Not that he'd care.

46:04.595 --> 46:08.056
Shit, he barely treats her like a person.

46:08.057 --> 46:10.100
Oh, it pisses me off.

46:12.687 --> 46:13.854
I know.

46:14.772 --> 46:18.317
I know all her medical bills would be
about 50 million won.

46:19.568 --> 46:21.862
Hospital, treatments, operation.

46:26.200 --> 46:27.285
I don't have that kind of money.

46:29.245 --> 46:31.204
I live paycheck to paycheck, too.

46:31.205 --> 46:32.498
I've got nothing.

46:46.095 --> 46:47.805
Hey, Heeju!

46:50.099 --> 46:51.100
Is that you?

46:52.143 --> 46:54.311
It is you!

46:54.312 --> 46:56.021
Long time, no see!

46:56.022 --> 46:58.065
It's me, Woogy.

46:59.859 --> 47:02.360
We both lived in that mining town
when we were kids.

47:02.361 --> 47:05.447
Sorry, I don't really...

47:05.448 --> 47:07.533
Sure you do. I was the kid with
the bald spot right here.

47:09.410 --> 47:11.286
What'cha doin'?

47:11.287 --> 47:13.456
You buyin' somethin'?
A ring?

47:14.373 --> 47:15.458
I can get you a good deal.

47:18.919 --> 47:21.464
Ah, damn.
It's been so long, right?

47:22.798 --> 47:26.510
We went to, uh, elementary school together
so it's been...

47:27.386 --> 47:28.803
...over ten years now?
:cue

47:31.223 --> 47:32.475
Okay, how 'bout Chan?

47:33.225 --> 47:35.936
Or Seonghun? You know, the kid who
followed you 'cause he liked you.

47:36.771 --> 47:38.272
No, I don't.

47:39.190 --> 47:40.900
Sorry, I don't remember.

47:49.450 --> 47:51.077
Well, that hurt my feelings a little.

47:51.827 --> 47:54.580
Hey, you really don't remember?

47:55.039 --> 47:56.165
'Cause I remember you.

47:58.417 --> 47:59.959
Wait, wait!
What about freeze tag?

47:59.960 --> 48:02.045
We used to always play
after school together.

48:02.046 --> 48:03.672
I'd get tagged and you'd unfreeze me.

48:04.340 --> 48:07.133
Maybe this'll jog your memory!
Freeze!

48:35.121 --> 48:36.622
I'll see you around!

49:11.740 --> 49:14.160
HAENGBOK PAWNSHOP

49:17.913 --> 49:21.125
'Kay, let me see.

49:25.254 --> 49:27.465
Yeah, this is real.

49:28.924 --> 49:31.384
How-how much you give for it?

49:31.385 --> 49:32.636
You don't need to know that.

49:33.929 --> 49:35.555
And they never came back for it?

49:35.556 --> 49:39.977
It's been over three months. Hmm.

49:43.564 --> 49:45.482
I'll give you 25 million.

49:45.483 --> 49:48.151
- We'll say 30 mill on the receipt, though.
-  Mr. Jang.

49:48.152 --> 49:51.447
All these years we've been doing business
and that's the best you can do?

49:52.406 --> 49:54.157
I'm being generous here.

49:54.158 --> 49:55.533
Collateral isn't worth market price.

49:55.534 --> 49:57.118
Just pay for the gold ring and get out.

49:57.119 --> 49:58.328
I can find someone else
on my own for this.

49:58.329 --> 49:59.370
All right, all right!

49:59.371 --> 50:01.164
All right.
All right, all right.

50:01.165 --> 50:02.665
I'll do it.

50:02.666 --> 50:04.209
I'll give you 27.

50:06.003 --> 50:08.213
You understand I need
to make money, too.

50:08.214 --> 50:09.839
30 million.

50:11.717 --> 50:13.343
Someone else already offered me 35.

50:13.344 --> 50:15.554
Okay, all right.
I'll pay you tomorrow.

50:17.056 --> 50:18.057
You drive a hard bargain.

50:28.484 --> 50:30.236
Ah, shit.

50:31.320 --> 50:32.947
Fucking bitch.

50:39.578 --> 50:41.413
Mr. Jang, wait.

50:42.331 --> 50:43.457
Who are you?

50:45.209 --> 50:48.254
I heard you trade in gold.
Do you?

50:48.796 --> 50:50.380
Yeah, I do.

50:50.381 --> 50:51.757
Which pawn shop are you with?

50:52.633 --> 50:54.634
Don't think we've met yet.

50:54.635 --> 50:57.512
If the piece is really big,
would you still buy it?

50:57.513 --> 51:00.306
Cast gold,
or something like a golden pig?

51:02.434 --> 51:03.893
A bar. A gold bar.

51:03.894 --> 51:05.896
A gold bar?

51:07.106 --> 51:09.608
Is it pure? How heavy?

51:12.152 --> 51:13.487
Ten?

51:14.154 --> 51:15.155
I'll buy it.

51:16.073 --> 51:17.283
I'd need to see it.

51:19.785 --> 51:21.953
How 'bout you get in the car.
Show me and we'll talk.

51:21.954 --> 51:23.037
No.

51:23.038 --> 51:27.585
Uh, could you just give me
an estimate, please?

51:28.252 --> 51:33.381
Sure. It's 580 won for 3.75 grams.

51:33.382 --> 51:35.842
So ten of those is 5.8 mil,

51:35.843 --> 51:37.969
but that's only if this whole thing
is above board.

51:37.970 --> 51:41.055
I guess since you came to me,

51:41.056 --> 51:43.391
you can't sell it at
a regular jewelry store.

51:43.392 --> 51:44.892
Am I right?

51:44.893 --> 51:48.438
My company, we can make a deal for 10.
100, even.

51:48.439 --> 51:51.733
If you're serious about selling
this thing, hop in. Then let's...

51:51.734 --> 51:52.818
Uh, I don't...

51:54.945 --> 51:56.155
I'll think about it a little more.

51:57.281 --> 51:59.408
You can't just bring this up
and then leave.

51:59.950 --> 52:01.535
At least let me have a look at it.

52:02.036 --> 52:03.786
- Let's see it.
- What?

52:03.787 --> 52:05.330
Is it in the bag here?

52:05.331 --> 52:08.791
- I told you I'd give you a good deal!
- Let go!

52:08.792 --> 52:09.751
Stop it!

52:11.337 --> 52:14.673
Ah, fuck, that stings!

52:15.382 --> 52:17.635
Why is everyone such
a fucking bitch today?

52:18.344 --> 52:20.511
:cue

52:25.142 --> 52:26.935
Where the hell have you been?

52:28.312 --> 52:30.648
Someone came asking
for you this morning. Some guy.

52:32.775 --> 52:33.858
Who was it?

52:33.859 --> 52:35.653
No idea.
That's why I'm asking.

52:36.570 --> 52:37.987
He said he lived in
the same town as us,

52:37.988 --> 52:39.156
but I don't recognize him.

52:39.823 --> 52:41.324
He seemed shady.

52:41.325 --> 52:44.036
Like one of those thugs who collect money
for loan sharks.

52:46.330 --> 52:48.039
Did you borrow money?

52:48.040 --> 52:49.666
Tell me you haven't been gambling.

52:49.667 --> 52:50.918
No, I'm not like you.

52:51.502 --> 52:52.544
I would never.

53:03.305 --> 53:04.681
TYLENOL

53:04.682 --> 53:05.891
What are you, sick?

53:06.850 --> 53:07.975
Have you been in pain?

53:07.976 --> 53:10.228
Doesn't matter.

53:12.940 --> 53:14.483
It's cancer, isn't it?

53:15.734 --> 53:17.528
Mija told you.

53:18.320 --> 53:19.655
Why didn't you tell me?

53:20.948 --> 53:22.783
You ran away 'cause you hate me.

53:24.118 --> 53:26.452
Then at least listen to Mija when
she tells you to go to the doctor.

53:26.453 --> 53:27.537
I did.

53:27.538 --> 53:28.789
I did go.

53:31.083 --> 53:33.877
Doctor said it was bone cancer
or something.

53:37.089 --> 53:38.673
Then we have to go back.

53:38.674 --> 53:41.217
Go back so we can find out
what stage it is,

53:41.218 --> 53:42.970
what treatments there are,
if you need surgery.

53:43.721 --> 53:45.972
Are you sitting around here like
an idiot just because of money?

53:45.973 --> 53:47.140
What's with you?

53:49.685 --> 53:51.394
We're going to the hospital tomorrow.

53:51.395 --> 53:53.980
I don't even have money for food.

53:53.981 --> 53:56.607
We'll figure out a way to make
the money later.

53:56.608 --> 53:58.569
Oh, is that how it works?

54:00.320 --> 54:02.740
If life were that easy,
why are we here?

54:05.117 --> 54:07.202
I've looked into
it more than enough.

54:08.537 --> 54:10.581
The doctors said I
was better off not knowing.

54:12.374 --> 54:14.334
The surgery might get me
a few more years.

54:15.419 --> 54:19.088
Or I could die now.
What's the difference?

54:19.089 --> 54:20.799
We're all gonna die anyway.

54:22.342 --> 54:24.803
Oh, I'm tired of living like this.

54:27.931 --> 54:30.558
Come on.
You don't really mean that, do you?

54:30.559 --> 54:33.186
We're going to the doctor tomorrow.

54:33.187 --> 54:34.604
Just let it go.

54:34.605 --> 54:38.441
You want me to call an ambulance?
I'm taking you one way or another.

54:38.442 --> 54:40.777
Be sure to lock the door
when you go to sleep.

54:40.778 --> 54:41.779
But...

54:50.162 --> 54:51.455
:cue

55:02.716 --> 55:04.342
HAENGBOK PAWNSHOP

57:08.592 --> 57:11.136
-  Who are you?
- Holy fuck, you scared me.

57:14.222 --> 57:15.681
You gotta be kidding.

57:15.682 --> 57:18.351
Everyone's walkin' around
with a gun lately.

57:18.352 --> 57:20.519
You know that shit's illegal, right?

57:20.520 --> 57:22.980
Get out or I'll scream.

57:22.981 --> 57:26.359
This isn't Seoul, Heeju.
You think anyone will come for you?

57:26.360 --> 57:27.860
I already called the police.

57:27.861 --> 57:29.488
Bullshit.

57:30.781 --> 57:33.074
The police?
You really want that?

57:34.868 --> 57:36.953
We met a few days ago.

57:37.871 --> 57:39.498
And I almost fucking died.

57:44.711 --> 57:48.005
The person in the van.
It was you.

57:48.006 --> 57:50.217
At first I wasn't so sure.

57:50.676 --> 57:52.344
But when I saw you on the street,
I knew.

57:53.929 --> 57:56.472
Don't act like you know me.
You're not my friend.

57:56.473 --> 57:58.642
Don't change the subject.

57:59.685 --> 58:00.769
Where's the casket?

58:02.646 --> 58:04.272
We found the van back at the warehouse.

58:05.357 --> 58:07.317
But the casket was missing.

58:08.694 --> 58:10.027
Tell me where it is.

58:11.405 --> 58:12.864
Ah.

58:14.574 --> 58:16.033
That it?

58:16.034 --> 58:17.702
Stay right there!

58:17.703 --> 58:19.037
I'm not afraid to shoot you.

58:20.831 --> 58:21.997
You sure it's loaded?

58:21.998 --> 58:24.125
You can find anything at a pawn shop.

58:24.126 --> 58:26.670
Do you really want to find out?

58:27.421 --> 58:28.504
Okay, okay.

58:28.505 --> 58:30.215
Yeah, I guess that's true.

58:31.508 --> 58:33.135
But just think for a sec.

58:34.052 --> 58:36.638
That stuff in the casket.
The drugs.

58:37.389 --> 58:38.473
Come on.

58:39.349 --> 58:40.559
Do you even know how to sell it?

58:41.476 --> 58:43.477
You can't do it alone.

58:43.478 --> 58:46.814
Lee Dokyung's basically crippled
after his accident.

58:46.815 --> 58:48.983
What good are the drugs to you, huh?

58:48.984 --> 58:50.694
If you can't sell 'em,
they're useless.

58:52.362 --> 58:54.448
- Heeju...
-  I said don't move!

58:55.657 --> 58:57.200
I came here to help you out, Heeju.

58:57.701 --> 59:00.327
If I wanted to hurt you,
I would have brought the others.

59:00.328 --> 59:01.746
Let's just talk, yeah?

59:01.747 --> 59:04.373
Don't-don't move!
I swear I'll shoot you!

59:04.374 --> 59:05.374
Put the gun down.

59:05.375 --> 59:07.168
I told you to stay!

59:09.671 --> 59:11.005
Ah, shit.

59:13.675 --> 59:16.470
I knew it.
You're a fuckin' liar.

59:22.726 --> 59:24.351
- Holy shit!
-  No, wait.

59:36.114 --> 59:38.283
Look, I tried to be nice, but shit.

59:39.201 --> 59:41.244
I'll fucking shank you,
so stay down.
:cue

59:44.915 --> 59:48.459
Why the fuck is this thing so heavy?

01:00:11.608 --> 01:00:13.443
Oh, fuck.

01:00:14.444 --> 01:00:15.445
Heeju.

01:00:17.531 --> 01:00:18.615
What is this?
